    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "CHARACTERFUL 3-BEDROOM VICTORIAN HOME | APPROX. 100m² | ATTIC CONVERSION | EXCELLENT CITY-CENTRE LOCATION\r\n\r\n4 Clonmore Terrace is a substantial 3-bedroom Victorian red-brick mid-terraced home, ideally positioned in a quiet and established residential setting in North Strand, Dublin 3.\r\n\r\nOffering approximately 100m² of accommodation, the property provides generous living space, three large double bedrooms and a converted attic, making it an excellent opportunity for a purchaser looking for a well-proportioned city home with scope to modernise and make their own.\r\n\r\nThe ground floor provides a welcoming entrance hall, spacious reception accommodation, dining area and kitchen. Upstairs are three generous double bedrooms and bathroom accommodation, while the converted attic provides valuable additional space for a home office, study, hobby room or other uses, subject to the necessary requirements.\r\n\r\nThe property's location is a particular highlight. Dublin city centre and the IFSC are within easy walking distance, while excellent public transport links provide convenient access throughout the city. Fairview, Clontarf and a wide range of local shops, cafés, restaurants and amenities are also close by.\r\n\r\nThe house retains the appeal and proportions associated with traditional Dublin Victorian terraces and offers a fantastic opportunity to create a home tailored to your own taste, while benefiting from an exceptionally convenient city location.\r\n\r\nViewing highly advised."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Substantial 3-bedroom Victorian red-brick terrace\r\n\r\nWithin walking distance of Dublin City Centre & Close to the IFSC and excellent public transport connections\r\n\r\nQuiet and established residential terrace\r\n\r\nHuge potential to improve\r\n\r\n3 double bedrooms\r\n\r\nGenerous reception and living accommodation\r\n\r\nExcellent opportunity to modernise and personalise\r\n\r\nConvenient to Fairview, Clontarf, shops, cafés, restaurants and local amenities"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "BER Details",
        "SortOrder": 4,
        "Content": "BER: E1"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Directions",
        "SortOrder": 5,
        "Content": "LOCATION\r\nClonmore Terrace enjoys an exceptionally convenient North Strand location, combining the character of an established residential street with easy access to Dublin city centre.\r\nThe IFSC, city centre, DART, Luas and numerous bus routes are all readily accessible, making the property particularly attractive to city-centre , owner-occupiers and buyers looking for a well-connected Dublin home."
      }
